review_comments:
```suggestion
        // TODO GH #4875: disable/customize this functionality
```

Shockingly, 

```c#

        String FontFace;
        Int32 FontSize;
```

in IControlSettings. Rather not touch that _obvious_ can of worms

I suppose I don't _need_ those, it just makes debugging the tests _infinitely_ easier. Simply just creating that object will enable `LogOnlyFailures` / `DisableVerifyExceptions`, you don't need to do anything else. I don't know how exactly it works, but it's handy for doing things like 

```c++
void SomeTest() {
    VERIFY_SOMETHING();
    {
        auto verifyOutputScope{ VerifyOutputSettings::LogOnlyFailures };
        for (int i = 0; i < 10000; i++) {
            doSomething();
            VERIFY_SOMETHING_ELSE();
        }
    }
    VERIFY_A_THIRD_THING();
}
```

now `VERIFY_SOMETHING` and `VERIFY_A_THIRD_THING` will definitely get printed, but `VERIFY_SOMETHING_ELSE` will only get printed when it fails, so you don't get 10000 lines of spew

